WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.973
- I feel like my heart's racing.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.843
Yeah, I literally can't even describe.

00:00:05.408 --> 00:00:07.030
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:07.940
I'm Lauren.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.113
- I'm Lizz, and today, we're gonna step inside North Korea.

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.010
We just got to Seoul,

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.200
and we're about to get on this tour bus

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.700
that's gonna take us all the way to the Joint Security Area

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.650
and actually get to step inside North Korea.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.143
North Korea has been in the political spotlight,

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.650
so I think getting to visit the border

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.810
is gonna be super eye-opening.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.690
- I just can't believe we're gonna go see this land

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.853
that, like, nobody gets to see, really.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.880
And this is where we're getting picked up.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.990
Everything's kind of confusing.

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.540
We have to find out where we're meeting our people.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.750
I think we just maybe wait around here.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.980
- Do they just know we wanna go?

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:46.973
'Cause we look confused.
- Yeah.

00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:49.219
- Your tour is this building.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:50.500
- [Lizz] We finally figure it out,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.123
and we all end up getting on this bus.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.157
There's our bus.

00:00:56.157 --> 00:00:58.657
(light music)

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.750
- So, our tour guide's name is Sky,

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.410
and she's hilarious.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:06.510
I'm obsessed with her.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.033
She said there might be a war at the end

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:11.750
because we have Americans, Japanese, and Chinese,

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:14.640
and if we speak too loudly, there's gonna be a war.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.540
- [Sky] Yeah, whispering only allowed.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:17.683
Yeah?

00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:19.700
If you interfere them, there's a chance,

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.703
end of the tour we could have a war.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:27.960
- So, right now, we're at the first stop,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.320
which is the Peace Park.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.410
There's all these ribbons all over this fence

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.803
that are written for wishes of peace.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:39.510
(light music)

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.990
We just walked across the Freedom Bridge,

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.733
but there's a gate that stops you at this other end.

00:01:47.927 --> 00:01:50.427
(light music)

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:59.083
- That's crazy.
- Wow.

00:01:59.487 --> 00:02:00.737
- [Lauren] Wow.

00:02:01.178 --> 00:02:04.210
(light bouncy music)

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.300
- I'm in the middle of eating lunch,

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.460
and I notice that Lauren has been gone a really long time.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.937
All of a sudden, I get a text from her that says,

00:02:09.937 --> 00:02:11.707
"Come outside right now."

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.823
Because apparently there's puppies.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:15.363
Oh my God!

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:18.820
- [Lauren] I just want 'em to come to me.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.497
- Wait, that's so cute.
- Come to my arms!

00:02:20.497 --> 00:02:21.757
I'm like, "Puppies, puppies!"

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:24.490
It was a nice little experience

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:27.203
before a very tense moment in our lives.

00:02:29.014 --> 00:02:30.970
(dramatic music)

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.040
- So, we get back on the bus

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.467
for about another 30 minutes, and they say,

00:02:34.467 --> 00:02:36.750
"All right, we are arriving at the JSA."

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:39.264
Like, they're starting to get more and more intense.

00:02:39.264 --> 00:02:42.014
(dramatic music)

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.640
As soon as we got to the first checkpoint,

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.380
they got really, really strict

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.640
about us not being able to take photos.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.970
- [Lauren] If we make some sudden movement

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:57.820
that the North Korean soldiers get offended by,

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.570
it's possible that we could be used

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.253
in propaganda video in North Korea.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.700
- [Lizz] And then they make us sign

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.510
this really intense waiver that says

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.410
they're not responsible for our death.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.980
- I'm honestly feeling pretty tense.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.487
I'm like, "Was this a smart move?

00:03:12.487 --> 00:03:13.807
"I'm not so sure."

00:03:14.657 --> 00:03:16.640
This is crazy.
- Are you recording?

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:17.740
- [Lauren] Yeah, I am.

00:03:18.013 --> 00:03:20.527
- I can't believe we're looking at this right now.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.430
It's so crazy in real life.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.670
- [Lauren] I was too scared to move my body too much,

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.973
and I'm just standing there thinking,

00:03:29.247 --> 00:03:30.643
"Don't do anything dumb.

00:03:30.717 --> 00:03:32.537
"Lauren, don't do anything dumb."

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:36.330
- It's weird those other guards are facing the wall.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.103
Literally, their faces are, like, in the wall like this.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.280
That's very strange.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:43.863
We only have one minute to take pictures.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.450
So they're about to make us stop.

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:46.734
- And we're whispering.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.815
- We have to whisper.
- I don't know why.

00:03:48.815 --> 00:03:50.274
- And they're really particular about where we can

00:03:50.274 --> 00:03:51.540
and cannot film.
- Alright, ladies, gentlemen,

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.055
we only have two minutes left!

00:03:53.055 --> 00:03:54.606
- Two minutes left.
- We have two minutes left!

00:03:54.606 --> 00:03:56.106
- It's so intense.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.743
I feel like my heart's racing.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.293
It's just crazy.

00:04:01.987 --> 00:04:03.160
Yeah, I literally can't even describe.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.323
- We had to walk up in two lines like this.

00:04:06.455 --> 00:04:07.763
I can't show that, sorry.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.410
So, then it's time for all of us to file inside.

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.333
So we get, once again, in a single file line,

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.480
and we walk into the first, like, blue house that we see.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.610
- [Lauren] And the guard says

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:22.010
that everything is being monitored,

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:24.720
and it's under surveillance 24/7

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.060
by these little microphones that are on the desk.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.360
- [Lizz] What was crazy is that,

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.610
when we looked outside the window,

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.713
we actually saw the North and South Korean border.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:34.102
- That's the border.

00:04:34.102 --> 00:04:35.310
Like, that's the border.

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.411
We're literally about to cross the border.

00:04:37.411 --> 00:04:40.161
(dramatic music)

00:04:43.344 --> 00:04:45.202
- Just did it.
- We're now in North Korea.

00:04:45.202 --> 00:04:46.557
- Now in North Korea.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.200
My mind is just totally blown.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.210
I can't believe I'm actually here.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:55.050
I've seen these houses in so many photos and documentaries.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.860
So, we basically just walked back and forth

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.240
between South Korea for the three minutes

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.750
that we had time for.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.163
- Yeah, I'm like, "North Korea, South Korea.

00:05:03.247 --> 00:05:06.740
"North Korea, South Korea."
- That's what we did.

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:08.823
- That's the JSA Jig.
- Yeah.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.800
It's incredible actually getting to step foot inside

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.270
of a country that I've heard so much about

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:17.363
and you read so much about on the news,

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.030
and to actually be there and feel it

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.130
and feel that tension

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.170
is just like nothing I've ever experienced before.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.450
- It's just like a crazy thing to actually experience it,

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.090
and you really could feel the tension.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.943
- Now that it's done and we're coming back,

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.920
the guard is making jokes.

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.190
We're all super chill.

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:35.600
We're allowed to take photos where weren't before,

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.745
and it feels like we just kind of overcame something.

00:05:37.745 --> 00:05:41.670
- Yeah, I do feel like, "We made it there and back!"

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.220
- My heart is beating.
- Yeah.

00:05:43.241 --> 00:05:45.824
(upbeat music)

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.950
I'm afraid I'm gonna do something wrong.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.830
At one point, I gave the thumbs up.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.157
I was just like, "Oh no, my thumbs up

00:05:54.157 --> 00:05:56.477
"is gonna start a world war."

